aw-thoughts/note-1","content":"This is an automated transcript of the first recording, with paragraph breaks added for readability. Please check uncertain wording against the recording."},"1304":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1-3","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1#transcript","content":"Okay, so I just want to essentially start this off by saying that with this book that's coming out, you have to understand that as I'm writing this book, I am very much so in debt. I'm blessed because I have a job. I work as a software engineer professionally, so I'm blessed because I have a job that I'm able to earn a lot of money, but I've made a lot of student financial decisions and I have credit card debt, I got student loans debt, but I'm writing this book because even with all of that, at the end of the day, this is something that God has told me to do and I feel like I have a lot of useful tips that could truly, truly help. I have a lot of useful tips that could be helpful for a lot of people because I've learned a lot about finance. I've tried to start, I've worked at a few different fintechs so I know how these apps work. I have built fintech apps before. I've also spent,"},"1305":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1-4","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1#transcript","content":"I don't know when this book is going to be released, but I'm also in the process of, actually I can talk about that later. Yeah, I currently work as an engineer at a fintech and so finances are stuff I think about a lot. I've done investing. My mom is a real estate investor. My friends and I, my friends, they buy and sell, they invest in stocks in the stock market. I have a father-in-law who's, don't talk about father-in-law, I have family who've also done, who've done well in business. I have a friend who's doing very well for himself. I have friends who are doing very well for themselves. I'm married. Depending on when this comes out, I may or may not have a kid, I don't know, but yeah, so just context to just understand the fact that I'm not talking about this on a place of arrogance or talking about this on a place of like, oh, like I've done, I've done my, I've done this shit. You"},"1306":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1-5","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1#transcript","content":"know what I'm saying? Like I'm also still trying to figure it out as well, but God has told me that I should write this book and that's what I'm going to do. And even if it's only one person that I'm able to help, then so be it. So moving forward, next to talk about is the fact that like, you know what, it's okay that you need to first ever, I think that's something that people need to understand in this life and figure out is the, I think that people need to like come to terms with the fact that like realistically not everybody is going to be a millionaire and that's not what, that's just not true. That's not factual."},"1307":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1-6","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-1#transcript","content":"That's not a possibility. And that's not something that everybody wants. It is not okay to shame people for not wanting to do that. Everyone has different goals and priorities. Everyone has different things that make them happier. Some people care about, some people want a lot of money because they want to be able to feel secure. Some people want a lot of money because they want to be able to go on vacations. Some people want to be well off just because they like cars and watches. Some people just want to be well off because of a medical, to be able to pay medical bills for the family and whatnot. So it's not, this is not about becoming a millionaire. That's not what this is for. This is just Oh my God."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","type":"page","content":"Note 2","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Raw thoughts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2"},"1309":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-0","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","content":"Working transcript of the second recording."},"1310":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-1","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2#transcript","content":"Transcript"},"1311":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-2","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","content":"This is an automated transcript of the second recording, with paragraph breaks added for readability. Please check uncertain wording against the recording."},"1312":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-3","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2#transcript","content":"Yeah, this book is not about making everyone become a millionaire. That's the furthest thing that this is about. This is just about making sure that regardless of the financial stage that you're in, I will go through those."},"1313":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-4","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2#transcript","content":"You have the right tools and knowledge at your disposal in order to be able to make wise financial decisions. Because the truth is that money is fluid. We have ups and we have downs."},"1314":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2-5","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-2#transcript","content":"There's times and years where someone has a lot of money and then there's times and years where you don't have a lot of money. You can very well off and you can lose it all. You can be in a lot of debt, you can win a lottery, it doesn't really matter."},"1