 your finances and think about the future if you're not earning money on a regular basis. And the truth is that, again, I feel like it's better for you to work at McDonald's or be a Uber driver or be a food delivery driver than to sit at home and not be making any money. If you're not a student full-time, if you're not like a student, sometimes you just can't"},"1425":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5-15","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5#0105820","content":"work and that's completely fine. Again of course, I think the only exceptions to this rule is that if you're a stay-at-home mom, because being a stay-at-home mom, that is your job, it's a full-time responsibility to be responsible for your children, or normally I'll say stay-at-home mom, stay-at-home parent. It's a full-time responsibility to be able to be responsible for your children while your partner is working all the time. And some people, this is what they want and that's completely fine. There's no negative aspect of being a stay-at-home parent because if that's what works for the dynamic of your relationship and if that's what you want for your life, that's completely fine. If that's not you, you need to have something that's getting you income every single week, month, something, something that's making you money."},"1426":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5-16","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5#0201000","content":"And I would suggest that even if it's temporary, even if it's temporary, just have something. And the truth is that applying to jobs, some people have this thing of like, \"Hey, I really want to work for a very specific type of company,\" and you're applying for jobs and your jobs that you could very well do, but because it's not the type of company that you want to work at, you just don't apply for them. You know what I'm saying? It doesn't make any sense, especially for those at the start of your career. Unfortunately it doesn't really make any sense for you to be picky and choose. It doesn't really make sense for you to be picky about the type of work that you want to have when you don't have anything right now. I'm so sorry. You don't have that choice. A lot of people are not going to like what I'm saying, but it's just the reality situation."},"1427":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5-17","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5#0304920","content":"You don't have the liberty of being picky. If you're not earning any income on a regular basis, like..."},"1428":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5-18","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-5#0304920","content":"Return to Raw thoughts."},"1429":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","type":"page","content":"Note 6","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Raw thoughts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6"},"1430":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-0","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","content":"A continuation on finding work and widening a job search."},"1431":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-1","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#wording-and-source-details-to-check","content":"Wording and source details to check"},"1432":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-2","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#transcript","content":"Transcript"},"1433":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-3","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0000000","content":"00:00.000"},"1434":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-4","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0100000","content":"01:00.000"},"1435":{"id":"