e.” The apparent contradiction was not resolved by a second automated pass. The primary wording remains unchanged."},"1441":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-11","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#wording-and-source-details-to-check","content":"The degree cost and job-search prescriptions are spoken examples and opinions; they are not verified facts about all graduates or all employment situations."},"1442":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-12","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0000000","content":"Yeah, the truth is that if you're not earning any—and a lot of you are not going to like what has—as I say this, if you're not going to like it—and that's fine. The truth is that if you're not earning any income, I'm so sorry, you do not have the right to be picky and choosing about what types of jobs you want to do. Apply for everything. Like, apply for everything. You never know. Like, it's better for you to work a job that you hate than to sit at home watching TV all day and be doing nothing. Like I said, except for if you're a student or like a stay-at-home parent, it just doesn't make sense, right? Especially as people who have—in addition, I'm speaking to people specifically who have a university degree."},"1443":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-13","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0100000","content":"Like, you have a degree you went to school for. You paid hundreds of thousands of dollars for your degree, but you're—and you don't have a job. And you're trying to pick and choose where you want to work, and you're not applying to certain companies because, \"Oh, it doesn't feel right,\" or, \"Oh, the salary's too low,\" or, \"Oh, it's—\" I would have to go into the office five days a week. Bro, suck it up. I'm so—like, suck it up and apply. Once you're there, you can work at a company for a month or two months and quit and figure out something else, but get some source of income. Like, you have to. Like, it's just—you have to. It's just what it is. Whether you like it or not, it's just the truth of the situation. When you're in a more comfortable—in a more comfortable position, then you have the liberty of being like, \"Oh, yeah, I don't want to work in this type of place."},"1444":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-14","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0201000","content":"I cannot pick and choose,\" because at the end of the day, you're still, like, earning something, right? So, yeah, I just wanted to say that and get that out of the way."},"1445":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6-15","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-6#0201000","content":"Return to Raw thoughts."},"1446":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","type":"page","content":"Note 7","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Raw thoughts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7"},"1447":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7-0","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","content":"Credit cards, borrowing costs, credit scores and payment records."},"1448":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7-1","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7#wording-and-source-details-to-check","content":"Wording and source details to check"},"1449":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7-2","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7#transcript","content":"Transcript"},"1450":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7-3","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7#0000000","content":"00:00.000"},"1451":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7-4","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-7","type":"heading","ta