e doing, you know what I'm saying, so, if you have signed a big contract, or you know there's money coming in, great, wait until the money comes in before you go and spend it, again, obviously the scenarios where like you have to make an emergency expense, like in the scenario where you want to buy tickets for a flight, and you don't have the money yet, and you haven't got paid yet, and"},"1567":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9-62","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9#2302080","content":"this applies to getting paid as well, don't go and say because I'm getting paid, don't go and say because I'm getting paid two grand next week for my paycheck, and she can't spend it now, nah bro, no, don't do that, it's a trap, it's a very easy trap that your mind will tell you is okay, but it's not, again, as I'm saying, you don't have to follow every single step, but these are just like tips and stuff that you should know, the thing I fall into this shit so many times, now this is actually the best opportunity to talk about buy now, pay later things, things like Karna, Affirm, things that are buy now, pay later, I see these things sort of how I feel, they're double edged sword, because what they allow you to do is that they allow you to have leverage, where you can spend money that you don't have here in order to be able to achieve results now, right, but the issue is that can you keep up with those payments, if you're already behind on your credit card payments, there's"},"1568":{"id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9-63","page_id":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/raw-thoughts/note-9#2400120","content":"absolutely no reason for you to be looking at fucking Karna or any of these buy now, pay later things, there's just no point, so that's it on buy now, pay later, keep them as credit cards, if you know that it's a cheap payment that you're not gonna really think about and feel, whenever it comes out