d reasoning, without a school-grade target, sentence-length limit, or comma limit."},"3113":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-15","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#voice-revision--october-1-2026","content":"The two opening pages and Chapters 1–8 have received a voice revision against Notes 1–9. The pass restores source-backed reactions, concrete situations, meaningful repetition, and admissions; moves transcript and production commentary to end notes; and preserves the worked examples, reader paths, financial qualifications, and workbook references. Chapters 9–12 remain planned rather than drafted."},"3114":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-16","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#voice-revision--october-1-2026","content":"Validation for this revision: the local production build passed, and all 524 checked internal links and anchors resolved. The bundled preservation check passed for all ten revised chapter/front-matter pages, including unchanged headings, tables, frontmatter, and original link targets. Number-count warnings were reviewed: they concern removed repetition and source-label wording, not changed calculations. Two chapter-editing workstreams were integrated and reviewed against the source notes; a separate read-only review checked the opening and Chapters 4 and 8. No CI run or publication was triggered."},"3115":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-17","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#voice-revision--october-1-2026","content":"A follow-up pass now covers the remaining technical explanations, worked-example commentary, transitions, and exercise instructions throughout Chapters 1–8. Exercises were rewritten as guided steps while preserving their required fields, decisions, exceptions, workbook references, and plain-paper alternatives. Strong passages from the first voice revision were retained. Tables and calculations remain unchanged. The follow-up passed the local production build, structural preservation checks for all eight chapters, and the internal-link check. Exercise requirements were compared with the previous drafts; the independent review caught and corrected a credit-limit wording issue before completion. No CI or publication was triggered."},"3116":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-18","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#voice-revision--october-1-2026","content":"The existing spoken scripts still reflect the earlier prose pass. Their examples and exercise references remain applicable, but their wording has not received this revision. The print PDFs are earlier layout proofs and do not include the revised Chapter 1 prose. Author review and later script/print synchronization remain."},"3117":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-19","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Source"},"3118":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-20","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Material to carry forward"},"3119":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-21","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Destination"},"3120":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-22","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Note 4, 00:00–04:25 and 08:45–15:23"},"3121":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-23","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Work backward from a desired life; use the invented Michelle example to include family time, satisfying work, purchases, saving, and household costs."},"3122":{"id":"/docs/writing-plan-24","page_id":"/docs/writing-plan","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/writing-plan#where-each-recording-goes","content":"Chapter 2, with a sho