ep the author's voice clear and direct.\" />"],[2255,"<Card title=\"Your mindset about money\" href=\"/docs/topics/money-mindset\" description=\"Know what matters to you.\" />"],[1586,"> debt is money that you are owing"],[1597,"> For chapter one, it's kind of crazy that we're asking people already about interest fees and stuff because we don't. I guess it's not that bad because we can just ask them to not feel worried about if they know it or not. If you know it, write it down. If you don't know it, then it's okay. And if you don't know the next payment, then it's okay. We're gonna review all these things later. It's just to get a full idea of where you're at right now."],[3261,"> I love cars, and I'm not going to pretend I don't care which one I drive. They make me happy. You might care about something completely different, and that's fine, because your quality of life matters too. But if getting the car means you can't enjoy driving it because you're worried about the payments, we need to look at that before you buy it."],[1594,"> I think for chapter one, you need to explain why the person has to have to see exactly what the total picture is. It's not to scare them. It's literally just because you can't make a plan if you're not able to see it. You need to actually see it, see it, like look at it. Like you have an amount, how much you owe, look at it. And then let's also to where it also asks them to write exactly how much they have, which I. Just write it on paper so you can actually see it, tangibly see it and get comfortable, like thinking about that number. And then there's also funds in which, like show them a paper, like checking your bank account or something like that, if there's any something we should."],[1591,"> I think for now it's not about if we need to make a page or not. Let's just still log it, but then um there could be sections and then we'll explain those things, like as we go. Like, I don't know what the best solution is here actually."],[160