ccurate, like— how do I put it— accurate mind map of exactly here, the different options that people have. It's one of these things. The same way in Alex Hormozi's books, he's like, there's only four ways for you to earn customers. It's this, this, this, or this. Everything else, everything falls into these four buckets. That's the kind of goal that we're trying to achieve here."],[3259,"> Sometimes you don't have enough money to pay all your bills. What happens then? I'm not going to sit here and pretend that never happens. When I'm in that situation, I look at what I absolutely need to pay."],[1600,"> Um, we can just get them to pick one here. We don't need to make a plan for both. It's just gonna get people confused. So if you have income and debt, you need to, first of all, I think— actually, I don't know what's the best thing to do here. I think that— gosh, I'm so tired. Okay, so I think that if you have income and debt, then let's go to what to do when you get paid first before we go to make a plan for your debt. Then in the income and no debt, you can go to the life you want. You can go to the life you want. And then for the no income and debt, let's just get them to find a job first, because, like, that's the most important thing, to make a plan for the debt yet. And then for the no income or no debt, we can still just go to the income. Let's go to also find and grow your income as well. That way it gives people a more direct guide on what to go for, on what to go into, on what the next steps are, and then, yeah."],[3253,"> We have ups and we have downs. You can earn a good income and still struggle to get to the next payday, so I want you to have something you can use wherever you are right now. Work through the part that fits your situation, put it into practice, and come back when you need the next part. You're probably not going to remember every single thing in here anyway."],[73,"−$1,100"],[1052,"−$1,125"],[1032,"−$1,250"],[420,"−$120"],[1030,"−$2,500"